§ `Annex XIV point 1: who may assess conformity, and the scope of a designation`

-- Point 1, first sentence (consolidated line 1963) says that the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems may require the involvement of conformity assessment bodies:
-- a statement of fact that creates no rule (inert, reason 1; NOTES.md, Coverage). The second and third sentences are operative.
-- src:1963 | Conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems pursuant to this Regulation may require the involvement of conformity assessment bodies. Only conformity assessment bodies that have been designated in accordance with this Regulation may carry out conformity assessments and only for the activities related to the types of AI systems concerned. The list of codes, categories, and corresponding types of AI systems sets the scope of the designation of conformity assessment bodies notified under Article 30.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Annex XIV point 1 (src:1963)
-- Gloss: only a body that has been designated under the Regulation may carry out a conformity assessment, and only for the AI systems of the types its designation covers.
GIVEN `the conformity assessment body has been designated in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities are related to the types of AI systems concerned by the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV as amended point 1 second sentence the conformity assessment body may carry out the conformity assessment` MEANS
        `the conformity assessment body has been designated in accordance with this Regulation`
    AND `the activities are related to the types of AI systems concerned by the designation`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only conformity assessment bodies that have been designated in accordance with this Regulation may carry out conformity assessments and only for the activities related to the types of AI systems concerned"

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conformity assessment body has been designated in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities are related to the types of AI systems concerned by the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV point 1 second sentence the conformity assessment body may carry out the conformity assessment` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the maybe-answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): Annex XIV was inserted by the Omnibus and is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST (`Annex XIV as amended point 1 second sentence the conformity assessment body may carry out the conformity assessment` `the conformity assessment body has been designated in accordance with this Regulation` `the activities are related to the types of AI systems concerned by the designation`))  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:1963 | Conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems pursuant to this Regulation may require the involvement of conformity assessment bodies. Only conformity assessment bodies that have been designated in accordance with this Regulation may carry out conformity assessments and only for the activities related to the types of AI systems concerned. The list of codes, categories, and corresponding types of AI systems sets the scope of the designation of conformity assessment bodies notified under Article 30.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Annex XIV point 1 (src:1963)
-- Gloss: the list of codes fixes what a designation covers: a type of AI systems is in the scope of a designation when the designation names its code. A code that is not on the list fixes no scope.
GIVEN `the codes of the designation` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the code of the type of AI systems concerned` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV as amended point 1 third sentence the type of AI systems is within the scope of the designation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Annex XIV as amended points 2 and 3 the code is on the list` `the code of the type of AI systems concerned`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a code that is not on the list of this Annex sets no scope under it
    ELSE JUST (any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS `the code of the type of AI systems concerned`) `the codes of the designation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The list of codes, categories, and corresponding types of AI systems sets the scope of the designation of conformity assessment bodies" (a definition by "sets": a code the designation does not name is outside its scope)

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the codes of the designation` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the code of the type of AI systems concerned` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV point 1 third sentence the type of AI systems is within the scope of the designation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): Annex XIV was inserted by the Omnibus and is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Annex XIV as amended point 1 third sentence the type of AI systems is within the scope of the designation` `the codes of the designation` `the code of the type of AI systems concerned`  -- VERSION as amended

§ `Annex XIV point 4: using the codes in the application for designation`

-- src:2010 | Conformity assessment bodies shall use the lists of codes, categories and corresponding types of AI systems set out in this Annex when specifying the types of AI systems in the application for designation referred to in Article 29.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Annex XIV point 4 (src:2010)
-- Gloss: a body that states in its application which types of AI systems it wants to be designated for does so with the codes of this Annex, and with no other. The application is the one of Article 29 (seam S-29, kept in P4-art-29-30).
GIVEN `the application for designation specifies types of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the codes used in the application to specify the types of AI systems` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV as amended point 4 the application for designation uses the codes of the lists` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application for designation specifies types of AI systems`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when specifying the types of AI systems in the application for designation" (fork F-unmet-where)
    ELSE JUST (   (NOT (`the codes used in the application to specify the types of AI systems` EQUALS EMPTY))
              AND all (GIVEN c YIELD `Annex XIV as amended points 2 and 3 the code is on the list` c) `the codes used in the application to specify the types of AI systems`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall use the lists of codes, categories and corresponding types of AI systems set out in this Annex when specifying the types of AI systems in the application for designation" (a bare "shall" not done)

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the application for designation specifies types of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the codes used in the application to specify the types of AI systems` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIV point 4 the application for designation uses the codes of the lists` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): Annex XIV was inserted by the Omnibus and is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Annex XIV as amended point 4 the application for designation uses the codes of the lists` `the application for designation specifies types of AI systems` `the codes used in the application to specify the types of AI systems`  -- VERSION as amended

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:2010 | Conformity assessment bodies shall use the lists of codes, categories and corresponding types of AI systems set out in this Annex when specifying the types of AI systems in the application for designation referred to in Article 29.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Annex XIV point 4 (src:2010)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Annex XIV party` `Annex XIV act`
`Annex XIV point 4 the duty of the conformity assessment body to use the lists of codes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted: Annex XIV is not in the text as enacted, so nothing is owed
         WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY `Annex XIV conformity assessment body`
             MUST `Annex XIV 4 use the lists of codes, categories and corresponding types of AI systems when specifying the types of AI systems in the application for designation`
             HENCE FULFILLED
